1
00:00:01,360 --> 00:00:02,060
Hello.

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:09,140
In this video, we're going to talk about
this section — the Setting Panel.

3
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:21,110
To put it simply, this is where we control
RiskPilot's behavior and its various settings.

4
00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:27,610
If you think of the panel itself as a car dashboard,
this part is the engine.

5
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:30,250
And we've put a lot of the settings in here.

6
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:46,290
I'm not going to run through every option
quickly in this video.

7
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:51,710
There are a lot of settings.
If I explained them all at once,

8
00:00:51,710 --> 00:00:56,190
it would probably be more confusing
and tiring than useful.

9
00:00:56,830 --> 00:01:03,240
That's why I've broken this section up,
and we'll make a separate video for each part.

10
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:15,480
If I were to list these options as headlines,

11
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:17,500
there are the appearance settings.

12
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:26,000
And then the panel size,
relative to the chart and the monitor.

13
00:01:32,090 --> 00:01:40,890
The On Chart section, which is very important,
connects directly to Presets — our saved settings.

14
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:48,060
We also have Manual — the manual settings —
so we can adjust things directly.

15
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:54,880
On Chart is explicitly linked to this part —
the Presets section,

16
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:57,400
which you set once and save.

17
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:14,130
Here we have the Guards section.

18
00:02:14,450 --> 00:02:18,670
It's especially useful for accounts
that work with prop firms.

19
00:02:19,070 --> 00:02:22,020
We can control our daily loss.

20
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:28,050
We can even set the spread,
and lock it at a specific level.

21
00:02:28,490 --> 00:02:33,130
And the number of trades per day,
to prevent overtrading.

22
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:52,370
We have the ATM section, which is very practical
and can run a really strong system.

23
00:02:57,130 --> 00:02:59,570
There's also ATR, in the same way.

24
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:09,600
This is the Pro section, as you're watching.

25
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,580
And this is Journal.

26
00:03:20,810 --> 00:03:23,790
And the rest of the items you're looking at

27
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:26,910
each have their own dedicated video.

28
00:03:27,510 --> 00:03:32,510
Watching each one can be useful,
depending on the strategy you use.

29
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:38,880
You can implement these kinds of smart models
and work in a very clean way.

30
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:45,490
The trader sets things once, according to
their own strategy and the plans they have in mind.

31
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:50,860
They set it once, and they know
these settings won't change.

32
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:12,300
If they need a fast scalping entry, it performs really well
for scalpers — and even Fast Scalpers.

33
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:18,270
Because they can use the panel settings
and come into this Manual Position section.

34
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:26,040
It can take that worry off the trader:
how much can I risk, what percent or how many dollars.

35
00:04:26,490 --> 00:04:31,780
Our account isn't always in a trend,
where we know: enter this much, exit at that much.

36
00:04:32,130 --> 00:04:39,420
A lot of the time we have to sit down and calculate
what percent is in a trade, what's growing, or what drawdown we have.

37
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:43,170
These are just a small part
of what this expert can do.

38
00:04:43,590 --> 00:04:51,770
It can be calculated once, the settings put in place,
and the trader can focus on more important things — not these calculations.

39
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:23,480
Thank you for your time.
All the best.

